  "strategy": "**1. Approach and Rationale**\nThe Erd\u0151s minimum overlap problem requires minimizing the maximum correlation between h(x) and (1-h(x+k)). Our approach leverages periodic comb structure optimization with intelligent parameterization to escape local optima. We represent h(x) as periodic combs with variable pulse widths and spacings, encoded as continuous parameters optimized by L-BFGS-B. The method balances adaptive mutation and rigorous gradient-based refinement to systematically explore lower C5 values.\n\n**2. Mathematical Specification**\n- **Representation**: Periodic comb function with:\n  - Pulse width parameter `w \u2208 [0.05, 1.0]`\n  - Pulse spacing parameter `s \u2208 [0.5, 2.0]`\n  - Duty cycle constraint: `(2.0-w)/s = 0.5` ensures integral of 0.5 over [0,2]\n\n**3. Implementation Procedure**\n**Stage 1: Initialization (0-20s)**\n- t0 = time.time()\n- Convert parent to comb parameters if available\n- Set resolution `n0 = 400 if parent else 300`\n- Use gradient-based refinement to initialize parameters\n\n**Stage 2: Mutation (20-900s)**\n- Maintain `(w, s, base)` triple representation\n- Perform adaptive mutations based on fitness:\n  - Wide-ranged w mutation when max correlation > 0.38\n  - Tight-waved s mutation when max correlation > 0.385\n  - Add \u00b10.02 to base when improvement stalls\n\n**Stage 3: Evaluation (each 60s)**\"\n- Build binary projection (0/1 array)\n- Compute correlation via `compute_c5`\n- Track best solution across resolutions\n\n**Stage 4: Termination (600-900s)**\n- Output best solution among 200, 400, 600 samples\n- Ensure exactly n_points/2 = sum(h) via projection\n- Verify min value is below 0.3808 threshold\n\n**4. Search Choices and Variations**\n- Base parameters: w=0.8, s=1.5, base=0.2\n- Mutation SD: 0.25 for w, 0.5 for s, 0.05 for base\n- Increase mutation range when:\n  - Correlation improvement < 0.0001 over 20 steps\n  - History of 8\u027fmax iterations\n\n**5. Budget and Resource Estimation**\n- Phase allocation: 20%(exploration), 80%(refinement)\n- Sample budget: ~5 x 600-point evaluations\n- Each fit evaluation: O(n_points*operations)\n- Use vectorized implementations for correlation\n\n**6. Validation and Return Contract**\n- Verify 0<=h[i]<=1 via projection\n- Compute shifted correlation scores\n- Return best h_values, C5_bound, n_points\n- Submit only if C5<0.3808",
